{
  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // PURPOSE: type-check the DEPLOYED SERVERLESS SURFACE — the repo-root `api/` shims
  //   and the handlers they re-export from `packages/cultivar-os/api/**`. Until
  //   2026-09-22 these files were in NO TypeScript project: `packages/cultivar-os/
  //   tsconfig.json` declares `"include": ["src"]`, `packages/trace-app` covers its
  //   own tree, and there is no root tsconfig. So `npm run verify` type-checked every
  //   screen and not one handler, while Vercel compiled all twelve on every deploy.
  // DEPENDENCIES: none — consumed by `scripts/verify-api-types.mjs` (ratcheted).
  // OUTPUTS: diagnostics only (`noEmit`). Tech-debt #77.
  //
  // 🔴 WHY THIS EXISTS, IN ONE INCIDENT: `api/discovery/ingest.ts` shipped a BARE
  //   RE-EXPORT of `callerHoldsPermission` and then called the name locally. A bare
  //   re-export creates no local binding, so every cost-apply request threw
  //   `ReferenceError`. A tsc over this project reports it as
  //   `TS2304: Cannot find name 'callerHoldsPermission'` — measured, by re-breaking
  //   the file. Nothing in the verify chain could see it, because the file was in no
  //   project. The two checks aimed at that gate both passed on the crash ([[R-33]]).
  //
  // ⚠️ `strict: true` MATCHES `packages/cultivar-os/tsconfig.json` AND IS LOAD-BEARING,
  //   NOT A PREFERENCE. Vercel finds no tsconfig and falls back to TypeScript's
  //   defaults, i.e. `strict: false` — and `strictNullChecks` is what makes narrowing
  //   on a BOOLEAN-LITERAL DISCRIMINANT work. Measured on this exact file set:
  //   strict false → 32 errors, strict true → 16. All 16 of the difference are
  //   discriminated-union false alarms (`if (!r.ok)` then `r.unmapped`) on code that
  //   narrows correctly. Lowering this flag re-manufactures all sixteen.
  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "lib": ["ES2020"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["api"]
}
